TI  - A unified architecture for customizable access to WAP content
T2  - 2008 PROCEEDINGS OF INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY AND ENVIRONMENTAL SYSTEM SCIENCES: ITESS 2008, VOL 2
CP  - International Conference on Informational Technology and Environmental System Science
AB  - Wireless Application Protocol is the result of convergence of mobile communication and Internet. It enables mobile users to browse WAP-enabled websites from a compatible mobile phone. The real-time, online, interactive characteristics make WAP a basic platform for a variety of mobile, value-added services. The rapid development of WAP applications is suffering the classic network-security and content-management problems of Web applications. Complying with the WAP architecture and its service model, this paper proposes a method for content security feature-enhancing on WAP gateway and devises the WAPCA protocol, a flexible interface and procedures, so that individual-based customizable WAP access can be easily achieved. A timeout-based scheme is introduced in WAPCA to provide QoS guarantee for WAP service. This architecture can be universally used to other content distribution system or be feature-enhanced with other functions. Our experiments validated the feasibility and performance of the presented mechanism.
