AU  - SHACKLOCK, PF
AU  - CROFT, GB
TI  - EFFECT OF GRAZERS ON CHONDRUS-CRISPUS IN CULTURE
T2  - AQUACULTURE
AB  - Gammarus oceanicus, Idotea baltica and Lacuna vincta grazed actively on C. crispus strain NRCC-T4 causing tissue damage characteristic for each species. I. baltica consumed approximately 20% of its body wt/day, G. oceanicus 5% and L. vincta 4%. These species can be controlled by various insecticides; dimethoate and malathion being effective between 1 and 10 ppm, diazinon and carbaryl at 1 ppm, and a mixture of rotenone and pyrethrins at 1 ppm and 0.4 ppm, respectively. The crustacean grazers were reduced by the introduction of fish predators, Salmo gairdneri, Gasterosteus aculeatus and Fundulus heteroclitus. All the grazers associated with C. crispus were killed when passed between rubber rollers.
